# Code owners for LEAPWare-ShellUX.
#
# This file exists so that review is ROUTED rather than noticed. Without it,
# a pull request waits for whoever happens to look; with it, GitHub requests a
# review from the owner of every changed path the moment the pull request opens,
# and a branch protection rule can require that review before merge.
#
# One owner, one line, because the project currently has one maintainer. That is
# a fact about today and not a decision to keep. THIS FILE NEEDS UPDATING WHEN
# THE TEAM GROWS: a single catch-all owner across a growing team stops being
# routing and becomes a bottleneck, and then a rubber stamp, which is worse than
# no rule at all. Split it by path at the point where more than one person can
# genuinely review each area — for example src/core/** to whoever owns the
# extension contract, docs/adr/** to whoever must approve an architectural
# decision, and scripts/** to whoever maintains the portability and citation
# gates.
#
# Note that the last matching pattern wins, so any future per-path line must be
# written BELOW this catch-all, not above it.

* @LEAPWare-Software
